function isPalindrome(str) {
    const cleanStr = str.replace(/\s+/g, '').toLowerCase();
    const reversedStr = cleanStr.split('').reverse().join('');
    return cleanStr === reversedStr;
}
```

To find the longest common prefix among an array of strings, you can use the following function:

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

string longestCommonPrefix(vector<string>& strs) {
    if (strs.empty()) return "";

    for (size_t i = 0; i < strs[0].size(); ++i) {
        char c = strs[0][i];
        for (size_t j = 1; j < strs.size(); ++j) {
            if (i >= strs[j].size() || strs[j][i] != c) {
                return strs[0].substr(0, i);
            }
        }
    }
    return strs[0];
}
```

This function works by iterating over each character of the first string and comparing it with the corresponding character in all other strings. If a mismatch is found, it returns the substring up to the current index as the longest common prefix. If no mismatch is found for the entire first string, then the entire first string is the common prefix.

